assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

`search_products` made one `GET /products` call and returned only that page. Vendor version 2026-10-01 now pages its results: for "cable" the first page has 5 items, `total: 7` and `next_cursor: "5"`, so the tool returned 5 of 7 matches. The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` until there is no next cursor, then returns all the items. The cursor parameter is already in the published spec. Old v1 responses have no `next_cursor`, so they still make one request and give the same output. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and the other 13 tests pass, but the repro test still fails. That's because the fix now asks for the second page (`GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5`), which the recording doesn't contain, and the test stops with UNMATCHED_REQUEST. It should pass once the call is re-recorded with `fiks rerecord`, which I couldn't run here because only the three pnpm commands are allowed. Separately, this recording also breaks the price range rule (prices like 6900 look like cents rather than dollars). That wasn't the target here, so I left it alone.

